@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+[
+  {
+    "file": "./styles/545-hard-candy.png",
+    "tool": "image_gen",
+    "reference_images": [],
+    "prompt": "Create ONE fresh image from text only, square 1024x1024. Use case: stylized-concept. The medium and visual style are the priority: a translucent hard-candy lollipop with a woman's portrait embedded IN glossy sugar glass. A macro confectionery still life: a thick round lollipop tilts diagonally on its pale stick in the foreground, with a softly blurred colorful candy shop behind it. The portrait is entirely handmade edible sugar art suspended within the candy, shaped from translucent colored sugar, with optical refraction, tiny bubbles, glassy glossy highlights and distorted edges; not a photograph printed on a candy. The woman is in her early 30s, with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, and a mustard-yellow knit sweater. Show an expressive stylized bust of her enjoying a tiny coffee cup, with a crescent croissant beside her within the candy design. The portrait proportions should suit decorative candy craft. Flowing swirls of pink, amber, turquoise and ruby sugar curl around her, colorful sprinkles caught within the sugar and scattered near the base. Rich light shines through the lollipop, beautiful transparent edges and warm refracted caustics, tactile candy shop atmosphere. Style determines all proportions, anatomy, framing, pose, palette and lighting. Do not reuse any composition or any previous image. No text, letters, captions, signatures, logos or watermarks anywhere."
+  },
+  {
+    "file": "./styles/546-truck-art.png",
+    "tool": "image_gen",
+    "reference_images": [],
+    "prompt": "Generate ONE fresh image from text alone. Square 1024x1024. Use case: stylized-concept. Authentic South Asian truck art: the fantastically decorated rear of a real cargo truck, seen in a low, wide rear three-quarter view so the tailgate is dominant while a little of the truck side and large wheels remain visible. Dazzling hand-painted enamel panels, dense ornamental scrolls, pairs of peacocks, roses and other flowers, concentric scalloped borders, cut reflective mirror chips, metal chains and dangling ornaments. Bold black outlines, flat saturated vermilion, emerald, cobalt, hot pink and yellow. The main TAILGATE PANEL contains a stylized hand-painted portrait of a woman in her early 30s enjoying coffee, in side-profile with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater. One hand raises the little cup to her lips; a croissant on a saucer is painted nearby within the same panel. Her anatomy and facial proportions must be charming vernacular truck-painter art with flat graphic shading and visible enamel brush strokes, not photoreal and not a photo transferred to the truck. Portrait is one integrated panel among profuse ornaments, not the whole image. A dusty roadside setting is peripheral; the splendid truck fills the square. Sunlight catches the mirror chips and worn metal. Let authentic truck decoration dictate composition, proportions and color. NO text anywhere, no script, lettering, numbers, license-plate characters, captions, signatures or watermarks; all areas that might carry lettering are filled with floral or geometric ornament instead. No reference images, no use of any prior image."
+  },
+  {
+    "file": "./styles/547-retablo.png",
+    "tool": "image_gen",
+    "reference_images": [],
+    "prompt": "Create ONE fresh 1024x1024 square image, from text only. Use case: illustration-story. A genuine-looking Mexican retablo ex-voto devotional folk painting on an aged square sheet of tin, presented straight-on with the tin filling almost all the frame: imperfect edges, two small nail holes, oxidation, scratched thin paint, humble hand-painted brushwork. The narrative scene fills the upper three quarters. In a simple café interior with intentionally awkward flattened perspective, a FULL-BODY small folk-art woman is miraculously saved from a spilled-coffee disaster. She is in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles rendered as simple dots, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater. Sitting sideways on a wooden café chair with her legs clearly visible, she holds a small intact coffee cup to enjoy it with a relieved smile; a tipped coffee pot on the adjacent table sends a dramatic brown arc of coffee toward her but a thin glowing miraculous ray diverts the spill away from her sweater and onto the floor. A croissant rests safely on a plate nearby. A small saint-like luminous apparition in a cloud occupies an upper corner, with a pale gold halo and delicate rays descending toward the coffee. Naive folk-art anatomy, uneven contours, stiff theatrical gesture, simple faces, skewed furniture scale, matte earth colors, faded ochre, brick red, dusty blue, aged cream and oxidized tin. Must look like a humble votive painting actually painted on metal, never a photographic café scene or digital cartoon. A broad cream-colored inscription area at the bottom is completely BLANK, unmarked, with aged surface only. No writing anywhere: no letters, captions, signatures, watermarks or numbers. Let the medium and folk-painting conventions govern all composition and proportions. Do not use any reference image or earlier image."
+  },
+  {
+    "file": "./styles/548-view-master.png",
+    "tool": "image_gen",
+    "reference_images": [],
+    "prompt": "Create ONE new 1024x1024 square image entirely from text. Use case: product-mockup. Retro toy photography, an unbranded red View-Master-style stereoscopic toy viewer and a separate round cardboard reel of tiny stereo photographic transparencies. A carefully composed diagonal overhead still life on a softly worn pale aqua tabletop: the chunky glossy red vintage plastic viewer sits in the upper-left, showing twin eyepieces, its slide lever and the slot for a reel; the ivory circular reel lies flat in the lower-right and partially overlaps a small warm light-table surface. Seven pairs of small rectangular photographic transparencies spaced around the reel with a central keyed hole, physically convincing vintage toy proportions. One slide window glows warmly from backlighting and is especially readable, while the other tiny slide windows remain darker. All the tiny pictures show café moments of a woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater, enjoying coffee with a croissant nearby. The highlighted slide shows her seated by a café window in three-quarter profile, coffee held near her smile, with the croissant on the table. She exists ONLY within these miniature film slides, not as a life-size person outside the toy. Fine film grain, little dust flecks and rich translucent amber slide colors, tactile cardboard fibers, slightly scuffed molded red plastic. Warm nostalgic 1970s analog product photograph, direct simple light and well-defined oblique shadows, uncluttered asymmetrical composition; toy and reel are the principal subjects, the woman a tiny image within the slide. No text of any kind, no brand wordmarks, no embossed letters, no slide numbering, no labels, no captions, signatures or watermarks. Render a blank red viewer and blank ivory reel apart from the slide windows. Fresh generation only; no reference images and no previous composition."
+  }
+]

